course: dictionary
lesson: 11250
title: Worsen: when things get worse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Worsen means to get worse, or to make something worse. «The storm worsened during the night» means the storm became more dangerous as the night went on. «Shouting will only worsen the problem» means shouting makes the problem bigger, not smaller.
explain: Read the words around worsen to find out which meaning is needed. Ask yourself: is something getting worse by itself, or is someone or something making it worse? Then swap in «got worse» and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Worsen often appears in health and safety. «Warning signs after a head injury include a worsening headache.» A worsening headache is one that keeps getting more painful, so a grown-up or doctor should be told straight away.
fact: Worsen is a verb. Its forms are worsen, worsens, worsened and worsening.
fact: «Worsened» means got worse, as in «the storm worsened during the night».
fact: The opposite of worsen is improve: when a problem improves, it gets better.
fact: «Worsening» can also describe a noun, as in «a worsening headache», meaning a headache that is getting worse.
fact: Worsen comes from worse, which is the comparative of bad. Worse means more bad.
exercise: «The storm worsened during the night.» What does worsened mean? | *Got worse | Became quieter | Got better | Stopped completely
exercise: «Shouting will only worsen the problem.» Does shouting make the problem better or worse? | Smaller | The same | *Worse | Better
exercise: Which word is the opposite of worsen? | *Improve | Wander | Stay | Worry
test: «If your cough worsens, see a doctor.» What should you do if your cough worsens? | *See a doctor or tell a grown-up | Hide it from everyone | Count to ten and try again | Ignore it and wait for it to stop
test: Which phrase means a problem gets worse slowly, bit by bit? | Suddenly disappear | *Steadily worsen | Happily grow | Quickly fix
exam: «Warning signs after a head injury include a worsening headache.» What does worsening mean here? | *Getting worse | Getting better | Going away | Feeling happy
